  "body": "Adds the `set_workholding_max_rpm` row to the camcraft-mcp skill's Setups section, and a note on `get_job`'s per-setup `workholding_max_rpm` field. Text only.\n\n**Row added** (after `load_machine`):\n\n> `set_workholding_max_rpm { \"max_rpm\": number | null, \"setup\"?: string }`: State the rated maximum rpm of a setup's chuck or collet; `null` clears it. Refused with a named error: a missing or non-numeric value, zero, negative or non-finite numbers, anything under 1 rpm or over 100000 rpm, an unknown setup, and a value the setup already states. `setup` defaults to the active one. One undo step. At post time, a constant-rpm (G97) turning operation faster than the limit is refused by name, and a constant-surface-speed (G96) section's rpm ceiling is capped at it (Fanuc `G50 S`, Tormach `G96 D`).\n\n**get_job note:** the description now ends \"... status), and each setup's `workholding_max_rpm` (its stated limit, or `null`).\"\n\n**Where each fact was read (main at 0fc30b65):**\n- Name, description, parameter schema (`max_rpm` required, `number|null`; `setup` optional string, defaults to active): `crates/app/src/mcp/workholding_tools.rs` lines 15-20 and 36-44.\n- Registration: `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs` line 69 (`super::workholding_tools::TOOLS`).\n- Missing / non-numeric `max_rpm` refusals and the one-step history call: `workholding_tools.rs` lines 23-31.\n- Active-setup default and unknown-setup refusal: `crates/app/src/mcp/setup_tools.rs` lines 66-72 (`setup_or_active`); no-declared-setup error at `workholding_tools.rs` line 29.\n- Zero / negative / non-finite / under 1 / over 100000 refusals: `crates/app/src/setup_workholding.rs` lines 31-45 (`MAX_STATED_RPM`, `invalid`).\n- Not-a-setup, no-op refusal, one undoable write with `invert`: `crates/app/src/commands/setup_workholding.rs` lines 28-43 and 63-70.\n- `null` clears (stated as `None`): `workholding_tools.rs` line 25; `commands/setup_workholding.rs` line 20-25.\n- Post time, G97 refusal by name: `crates/app/src/setup_workholding.rs` lines 68-105 (`program_problems`); G96 cap: lines 56-66 (`css_of`, min of tool and workholding, posts take min with machine).\n- get_job field: `crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs` line 64; `null` when none (`and_then`/`map`).\n\n**PROCESS_VERSION:** 26 -> 28 (main reads 26; PR #1191's open PR claims 27). The merger renumbers if needed.\n\n**What a fork must do:** pull the process files. Run `git fetch upstream --tags` then `git checkout upstream/main -- AGENTS.md .claude/agents .claude/skills .claude/PROCESS_VERSION xtask .cargo/config.toml scripts/gate.ps1 scripts/gate.sh scripts/release.ps1 scripts/collect-decisions.ps1 scripts/collect-decisions.sh`, commit as `chore(process): sync process files to upstream PROCESS_VERSION 28` on a `process-sync` branch, and merge it into `main` (per AGENTS.md \"Process files sync on every session\"). Details in the pinned issue #681.\n\nFiles only, no build. No cargo command was run.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1059\n",
